    "turn_idx": 77,
    "turn_text": "Absolutely. I mean, Godly and joyous to work at spring to mine. They're just wonderful, loving people. You can just feel their heart, you know. It's just people that care. And they are folks that you want in your community because they care about things greater than they are. And you can't give a person a more wonderful compliment than a world in a better place where you win it. And that goes for both Rode and Bianca. Without them being actively involved, You know, who knows what would have happened because would the chair of the Senate Criminal Justice Committee, would he have felt so passionately about it or not? I don't know. Maybe he doesn't even know. So meeting with me and lighting that spark for me, it was always a priority or office, one of our top priorities, but it became the number one priority after I met with him. And, you know, I talked to James Frank, my colleague and good friend in the house. It was also, you know, one of his top priorities. And it's that personal touch like with many things. But the thing that again, I admire so much about them is they channeled their grief into a passion to protect others.",
