    "turn_idx": 86,
    "turn_text": "talking about the bill right now, you know, they came to this case occasionally. And they came to the Senate floor and they were up in the gallery. And I, you know, we do recognition for our constituents on occasion. And I recognize them. And I thought I was just going to be very short recognition. Hey, they're here. This is what tragically happened to them. But this is the bill that we're, you know, trying to pass. And I was just so overwhelmed and overcome with emotion. It was very difficult to even speak. And you could just feel that everything on the Senate floor that day went by the wayside. All of our play differences, all of the, you know, the contrast, the differences and priorities just from washed away. And we were all focused on two human beings and two parents that have gone through one of the worst possible tragedy anybody can face and endure. And all we had, we were unified 31 parts, beating as one, looking up at them with tears in our eyes and a quiver in our voice, saying that we love you, we appreciate you, and we're going to do right by it.",
